/T (At the 6.0 kg design mass, the reference total lift-rotor thrust is approximately 26.7 N, corresponding to a thrust-to-weight ratio of 1.2 under Martian gravity. The report estimates roughly 960 W for total hover power and around 290 W of peak pusher demand during transition, compared with approximately 96 W of shaft power during steady cruise. Transition is much more demanding than cruising: the preliminary model allocates about 18 Wh to takeoff, transition and landing together.)
