/T (The concept relies on IMU measurements and visual odometry for relative motion estimation because Mars has no usable GNSS constellation or dependable global magnetic reference. RFD868x-EU radio is identified as a prototype communications component for aircraft status and telemetry; image datasets may need local recording rather than continuous transmission. Sensor measurements, image frames, timestamps and position estimates must be associated before map fusion. All specified electronics are Earth-analog candidate hardware and still require low-pressure, thermal, dust and radiation qualification.)
/E (The concept relies on IMU measurements and visual odometry for relative motion estimation because Mars has no usable GNSS constellation or dependable global magnetic reference. RFD868x-EU radio is identified as a prototype communications component for aircraft status and telemetry; image datasets may need local recording rather than continuous transmission. Sensor measurements, image frames, timestamps and position estimates must be associated before map fusion. All specified electronics are Earth-analog candidate hardware and still require low-pressure, thermal, dust and radiation qualification.)
