/Title (The concept relies on IMU measurements and visual odometry for relative motion estimation because Mars has no usable GNSS constellation or dependable global magnetic reference. RFD868x-EU radio is identified as a prototype communications component for aircraft status and telemetry; image datasets may need local recording rather than continuous transmission. Sensor measurements, image frames, timestamps and position estimates must be associated before map fusion. All specified electronics are Earth-analog candidate hardware and still require low-pressure, thermal, dust and radiation qualification.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 429 0 R
/First 507 0 R
/Last 507 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 477 0 R
>>
endobj
477 0 obj
<<
/Title (A restart or failure of the mission computer must not interrupt the real-time flight controller. Sensor fusion, fault handling, GNSS-denied navigation and end-to-end data reliability remain verification objectives.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 429 0 R
/Prev 476 0 R
>>
endobj
478 0 obj
<<
/Title (Mission planning begins with a candidate route over the prepared orbital map. During the proposed survey, the UAV would gather imagery, ground range and motion data. These observations must be spatially registered before rock clusters, surface irregularities and local elevation changes can influence the map. The planner distinguishes traversable, caution and high-risk areas, while locations lacking reliable measurements remain uncertain. A feature visible in only one frame should not automatically become a confirmed physical obstacle.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 430 0 R
>>
endobj
