527 0 obj
<<
/Title (During takeoff, the lift rotors provide vertical thrust. The pusher then accelerates the aircraft while rotor thrust is reduced as the wing starts carrying the load. The reference design assumes a stall speed of 18.8 m/s and a cruise speed of 24 m/s \(86 km/h\). Full rotor shutdown is therefore proposed only after adequate speed margin is achieved. Landing reverses the sequence. These are analytically modeled operating phases, not demonstrated Mars flight performance.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 526 0 R
>>
endobj
